From 507e45b1b2fe0407104c82359ca057f86d92de0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: znyrvalt <220587351+znyrvalt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 07:32:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] crossplay: fix GUI icon projection (canvas-relative
 units, auto-fit oversized models)

The first icons exposed a projection bug: _project worked in model-relative
units - it hardcoded the classic 16-unit item grid as the projection basis, so
every model was drawn at one fixed scale, and any model whose gui-projected
bounds exceeded the canvas ran straight past it (pureblade, hyperion,
dragonrend, frost_scythe and shadowblade all clipped).

The projection is now computed in canvas-relative units:

- the canvas is the basis - CANVAS_UNITS (16.0) canvas units span the drawable
  area, so the base scale belongs to the canvas, not to any model's grid
- after centering, each model's projected bounds are measured against that
  canvas; a model wider or taller than the drawable area is auto-fitted with
  one uniform scale factor (scale-to-fit, aspect ratio preserved - oversized
  weapon and ability models shrink to fit, they never clip and never stretch)
- models that already fit keep the canvas base scale, so small items do not
  balloon

Validator: new check 25 pins the guarantee (every rendered 3D icon keeps a
one-pixel clear border; flat full-bleed sprites are exempt by their inventory
model_kind). 30 checks, 3 failed - the two UV checks and the empty boneblade
icon are the remaining known issues, fixed next.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
